{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And behold, from the river there came up seven cows.</b> The sustenance of the land of Egypt was from the river, as it is written (Isaiah 19:7): ״ערות על יאור על פי יאור וכל מזרע יאור יבש נדף ואיננו״. And it is written (ibid.): ״ואנו הדייגים ואבלו כל משליכי ביאור חכה״. And it is written (ibid.): ״ובושו עובדי פשתים שריקות״. And it is written (ibid.): ״והיו שתותיה מדכאים״ etc." "<b>And they grazed in the marsh-grass.</b> The letter ב׳ is superfluous, as in (Proverbs 9:5): ״לכו לחמו בלחמי ושתו ביין מסכתי״ — for אחו is the name of the grass itself, as in (Job 8:11): ״ישגא אחו בלי מים״; and the sense of ותרעינה אחו — without the ב׳ — is that along the bank of the river they were grazing the אחו."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:19:08.256902160Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}